// `2b4m check <file> <theorem>` proves ONLY the named theorem (and what it cites): `good`
// checks alone even though `broken` (a mis-cited fact) fails, and the whole file fails.
pred p
pred q
axiom pq: p

theorem good: p
proof
  @conclusion |
    p
    [by cite pq]
qed

theorem broken: q
proof
  @conclusion |
    q
    [by cite pq]
qed
